jobs.prompt:
Edit ONLY the currently EMPTY BOTTOM NAVIGATION DOCK of the FIRST supplied image, the Wortkette game screen. Every pixel above the thin gold rule at the top of that dock should remain visually unchanged: same Korean and German words, numbers, typography, positions, header, current-word blocks, input, Senden button and shadows. Keep the same portrait canvas and crop. Do not alter the header or add a cloud.

The SECOND supplied image is the APPROVED Wörter-Quiz screenshot: use ONLY its bottom five-icon navigation as the visual reference. The next FIVE supplied images are the actual individual approved navigation icon sources, in exact left-to-right order:
1 calendar with two brass rings and six square day tiles, ivory on teal = Heute;
2 open ivory book with red center bookmark = Lernen;
3 worn muted-blue game controller, ivory plus pad and two warm gold/terracotta round buttons = Spiele;
4 Korean hanok front gate with dark blue tiled roof and green doors = Hanok;
5 three rounded human figures: blue left, terracotta head/teal body center, golden right = Gye.

Place precisely these FIVE icon designs in that exact order in the existing bottom emerald dock, at equal horizontal slot centers approximately 10%, 30%, 50%, 70%, 90% of screen width. Respect the approved reference's natural relative scales and materials; all icons fit fully within the dock, with comfortable top and bottom clearance. Treat their source PNG backgrounds as transparent, not black rectangles. Never substitute generic line icons, emoji, a house, a different controller, text initials, a closed book, or new artwork.

The THIRD slot (Spiele, game controller) is selected. Give ONLY that slot the same raised dark emerald rounded-square selection face, thin warm gold outline and subtle contact shadow as the approved screenshot. The other four icons have no selection outline. No icon labels or words under the icons. No extra icons, separators, badges, counters, dots, clouds, coins or settings gear. Keep the dock's existing thin gold top rule and the clear space between the Senden shadow and dock.

This is strictly a five-tab navigation completion edit. Do not change or regenerate any learning content, control or other layout. Output ONE full mobile screenshot, not a montage or a component sheet.

